    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0166" n="152" xml:id="pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/8–2544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-25T08:00:00+07:00">August 25, 1944—8
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 28—1:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1455. Naval Attaché states he now has reports from three separate Chinese sources
                    regarding holding of military conferences designed to reform Chinese Army (re
                    telegram 1432, August 19th) which are expected to terminate in about a week.
                    Press announcement today of appointment new director [of] Conscription
                    Administration [of] War Ministry<anchor n="59" xml:id="d139-f1"/> presumably
                    result of conferences.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d139-f1" n="59" xml:id="d139-f1-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Hsu Sze-ping.</p>
